  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Samoa - Procurement Reforms and Capacity Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot; The overall objective of the proposed IDF grant is to support the implementation of public procurement reforms and procurement capacity building, through the provision of technical assistance.  Such technical assistance would be utilized to further develop the procurement guidelines, and prepare procurement manuals, along with standard procurement.  Through the development of these documents and their adoption by the Government, it is envisaged that there would be significant efficiency gains in processing public procurement, and more transparency in the award of contracts. (Since a PAD is not prepared for IDF operations, the information was taken/adapted from the document &quot;&quot;Request for IDF Financing&quot;&quot;). DO: To support the implementation of public procurement reforms and procurement capacity building.  Outcome 1: Revision of the Government&apos;s Procurement Guidelines;  Outcome 2: Preparation and utilization Procurement Manuals, along with standard procurement documents  Outcome 3: Capacity development of Government officials in public procurement&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
